{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"STANDARD SET BY THE OPERATOR: 'the implicit acceptance criteria is shipping defect free code.'\n\nThat resolves the scope call I was hedging and REVERSES my own classification of two tickets. The test\nis not 'is it DC-specific?' or 'did this epic introduce it?' — it is 'does the code we are shipping\ncarry known defects?'. Under that standard:\n\n IN SCOPE, reclassified from 'defensible follow-up':\n * [rebar:387d-09c5-3d50-4a1e] a failed identity write DELETES the created issue.\n * [rebar:7c26-4ac8-04a3-440e] bindings key on the Jira KEY, which changes on project move.\n   I had argued these were out of scope because they are pre-existing and not DC-specific. That\n   reasoning does not survive the standard: shipping DC support ships those code paths to a NEW\n   deployment type, and 'we did not introduce it' is not the same as 'it is not a defect in what we\n   ship'.\n\n ALREADY IN SCOPE:\n * [rebar:21fc-51d7-90ca-4a03] DC index lag -> duplicate Jira issues. Data corruption, DC-specific.\n * [rebar:f391-806b-938f-45d8] the harness exhausts the 10-PAT cap. Not shipped code, but it degrades\n   the oracle every other criterion depends on.\n\n STILL ARGUING SCOPE, and flagging rather than deciding unilaterally:\n * [rebar:b586-2fda-8a15-4260] DC rate limiting. This is an ABSENT FEATURE rather than a defect: the\n   limiter is off by default, admin-enabled, DC-only, and the remedy is header-reactive. I have put\n   the argument to the operator rather than quietly adopting the convenient reading.\n\nPLUS the unmet headline AC recorded in my previous comment: no live evidence yet that bidirectional\nreconciliation MOVES DATA. 'scanned=0 ... converged' proves the pass runs on an EMPTY instance.\n\nSo the epic does not close on story completion. It closes when the shipped code is defect-free AND the\nbidirectional criterion has real evidence behind it."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785509526616349001,"uuid":"0d1f781e-f54f-47ef-bd71-ca316389f30d"}